diagnosis_text:
After exhaustive live inspection of every component along the pc1→pc2 data path, no fault was found. The simple_bgp topology is operating entirely correctly. The eBGP session between router1 (AS 1) and router2 (AS 2) is fully established and stable, with the correct prefixes (195.11.14.0/24 and 200.1.1.0/24) installed in each router's FIB via BGP. IP forwarding is enabled on both routers. No packet-dropping mechanisms were found anywhere on the path: all six interfaces across the four devices have zero RX/TX drop and error counters; no tc netem or rate-limiting qdisc is configured on any interface (only the default fq_codel); no iptables or nftables DROP/REJECT rules exist in any table or chain; RPF filtering is disabled; ICMP rate-limiting is disabled. Multiple independent ping tests — 5, 9, and 15 packets from pc1 to pc2, plus 15 in the reverse direction, plus 10 router-to-router — all completed with exactly 0% packet loss. The reported symptom (roughly one-third of pings timing out) cannot be reproduced at the time of investigation and has no corresponding evidence anywhere in interface counters, tc statistics, or firewall state. The root cause of the helpdesk complaint is a false premise: there is no injected or spontaneous fault in this lab. No corrective action is required; the network should be confirmed healthy and the ticket closed.
=== END ===